  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "Each project row now has a Delete button. It opens a confirmation dialog, and confirming removes the row and shows a \"Deleted “…”\" toast. I tested it in headless Chrome at 390px (phone) and 1280px (desktop), and both widths behaved the same.\n\n- **Confirmation:** The dialog uses the existing `Dialog` component with the danger style, and names the project in its message. Focus starts on Cancel.\n- **Cancel and Escape:** Both close the dialog and leave all 5 rows in place.\n- **Confirm:** The row is removed and the toast appears.\n- **Empty state:** Deleting every project shows \"No projects yet.\"\n- **Long names:** The longest name, `Supercalifragilistic…_API`, wraps without horizontal scroll. The button stays full-size and on-screen. The dialog and toast fit the viewport.\n- **Persistence:** Deletes are not saved. The list lives in `window.PROJECTS`, so a reload brings every project back. There's no backend or storage in this app, so I didn't add any.\n\nThe changes are in `app.js` and one line in `styles.css`. The existing static tests still pass. I also stopped the dev server and Chrome I'd started. My check script and screenshots are in the scratchpad folder, not the project.",
